My conclusion

Do not move Zentory to Robinhood Chain, clone Twofold, build another stock basket, or launch a high-APR staking token.

The strongest gap I found is a market-hours-aware liquidity protocol for Stock Tokens:

Wall Street closes. Onchain markets do not. The liquidity pool should know the difference.

Working codename: GapSafe—the name and ticker still need trademark and collision checks.

It would be a Uniswap v4 hook/router that automatically adjusts trading fees and protections when:

The referenced stock market is closed.
The Chainlink price is stale or uncertain.
The pool price diverges materially from the reference price.
Liquidity becomes dangerously thin.
A dividend, split, halt, or other corporate action is pending.

This is understandable in one sentence, solves a real problem, has protocol revenue, and is materially different from the projects already flooding Robinhood Chain. It cannot guarantee a large market cap—nothing honest can—but it has a better chance of generating durable attention than another reflexive token loop.

