Contract mechanism

For an initial Stock Token/USDG pool:

Verify the canonical token address against Robinhood’s registry.
Read the Chainlink reference feed.
Read uiMultiplier() and corporate-action state.
Determine the underlying market session.
Calculate a dynamic fee:
$$ \text{fee} = \text{base fee} + \alpha(\text{volatility}) + \beta(\text{price divergence}) + \gamma(\text{closed-session risk}) $$
Send most of the incremental risk fee to LPs and retain a small transparent protocol component.
Enter guarded mode if the feed is stale, a corporate action is unresolved, or divergence exceeds tested limits.

During normal hours, fees remain competitive. During dangerous periods, traders can still execute, but LPs are compensated for carrying additional adverse-selection risk.

The first version should adjust fees only. Hard trade caps or automated halts should come later because they introduce more failure modes and governance questions.

