Token design

My strong recommendation is:

Launch the dashboard and hook before launching the token.

A token going up can attract users, but launching it before the mechanism works creates the exact credibility problem you said you wanted to avoid.

If a token is required at beta launch, it should have genuine operational utility:

Pool deployers bond it to create supported markets.
Keepers bond it and can be slashed for provably incorrect updates.
Router users locking it receive fee discounts.
Governance controls bounded parameters, never arbitrary treasury withdrawals.
No passive “stake token, earn more token” loop.
No transfer tax.
No rebasing.
No unlimited minting.
No hidden blacklist or owner-controlled trading switch.

